<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhanga</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gitarama</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhanga, formerly Gitarama, is a town in the Southern Province of Rwanda, west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kigali">Kigali</a>. It was the home base of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gregoire-kayibanda">Grégoire Kayibanda</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hutu">Hutu</a> party <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parmehutu">Parmehutu</a>. On 28 January 1961 Hutu leaders meeting there proclaimed the abolition of the monarchy and a republic, the so-called Gitarama coup, which a referendum confirmed later that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muhanga.jpg" alt="Muhanga" width="320" height="139" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SteveRwanda · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GitaramaCityCropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
